  {
    "episode_id": 74506,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74506.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 16,
    "turn_text": "And Brandon, look, I've been up in these towers in regard to the state of technology. They literally have a paper strip that represents each flight. And so if you're doing one radius from the tower, And there's a coworker next to you who's doing the next radius out from the tower. You literally hand that slip of paper and say, hey, here's Southwest Flight 812 and handing it over because they're now going into that other person's radius or area. And I always think about what happens if you drop the paper? Like it's just frightening. That's how we're managing our air traffic control system in 2024. And so this is all about newer technology, more efficiency, better safety, and really excited about this being signed into law. And I think we're going to see another strong bipartisan vote in the House as we pass this final version that will be going on for the President's signature in coming days.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
