  {
    "episode_id": 74506,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74506.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 20,
    "turn_text": "So it's actually a pretty in-depth process. A lot of people have seen on TV these congressional hearings, and that is part of it. Bringing in witnesses, whether it's airline pilots, whether it's air traffic controllers, whether it's private pilots, whether it's innovators, folks are building aircraft, safety experts, bringing in all these people and having the experts come testify before Congress. And of course, that's a little bit more public facing, but we also literally had thousands and thousands of meetings with different stakeholders and maybe it's groups and individuals who had awful flying experiences, people who had new technology ideas, folks who are trying to develop that next generation drone or advanced air mobility system really just hearing from all these folks and we kept a list and ultimately at the end of the day we even submitted a solicited input from different stakeholders and members of Congress received over 2,000 unique submissions and just plowed through those over months and we're able to begin Organizing putting the outline of a bill together and ultimately getting it passed through the house with a strong margin. And then unfortunately we did that in June and again took the Senate until now to finally get a bill out of the Senate and to sit down and negotiate with us. We've been negotiating with the Senate in earnest since March and finally have a negotiated project between the House and the Senate. that we're really excited. So again, over two years, just to make sure that we get it right, that we're talking to the right experts. The last thing in the world you want is somebody who just got elected to Congress who thinks they understand something, who's out there writing a law and doesn't fully understand something in a way that could impact safety, impact efficiency, impact the gold standard of innovation and safety that we maintain in the United States. And so that's why you got to spend a good bit of time really making sure that you understand issues and that you're prescribing the right solution. Thanks.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "The legislative process described was very detailed and thorough.",
        "confidence": 0.96
