    "turn_idx": 42,
    "turn_text": "We're going to be, we're going to be taking up new legislation on the core of engineers within the next month. And just to remind you and others, some of these important flood protection projects like the Cobine Project, which benefits the entire capital region, just north of Baton Rouge that's under construction right now. It's going to be a game changer in regard to the entire plumbing for South Louisiana, or at least the southeastern portion of the state, every town from St. Francisville, South on the east side of the river, all the way down to Lake Morapaw. It actually drains into Lake Morapaw, not into Lake Morapaw Lake Pontchartrain, not into the Mississippi River. This new project will change that, giving more drainage capacity faster drainage capacity to that entire region. And so we're going to be working on that project and making sure it gets built and built efficiently. Going to be moving forward on massive coastal restoration efforts, hurricane protection projects. Of course, dredging our waterways and accessing our ports is a high priority. Louisiana has some of the top ports in the nation because of the Mississippi River system. But we are actually losing ground right now. to other ports on the east coast like Savannah and Charleston. We're losing ground to some of the ports, even like ports of Mobile, Gulfport, Houston that are taking traffic from us. We can't allow that to happen. We're not properly integrating all of the ports everywhere from Plaquemines Parish to St. Bernard to New Orleans, the Port of South Louisiana, the Port of Baton Rouge. It's all these fiefdoms today. We've got to make sure that we're managing those in a way that benefits the state holistically, and it's really important that we have the opportunity to maximize Louisiana's winds and maximize some of the experiences we've had to just let Louisiana let the nation experience the transportation system and the resiliency system that we truly deserve.",
