    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74506.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 46,
    "turn_text": "It doesn't make sense. And in many cases, this whole thing has just been confused by renewable energy sources, which I want to be clear. I'm fully supportive of things like wind and solar and wave and geothermal and nuclear, when they make sense. And they do in some applications, but trying to force them and trying to distort energy markets by driving up the cost of oil and gas, trying to cause those energy sources to be closer in costs to things like wind and solar just doesn't make sense in addition to the billions and billions of dollars in subsidies. I'll say it again, all of those energy sources have a place, but they've got to be used in the right applications and not forced in cases and also not going in a direction that makes us, instead of being dependent upon our own energy, reserves and our own energy resources, turning the countries like China and being beholden to them for things like solar panels, wind turbines, battery storage technology and other things, which clearly China is not an ally and has proven, for example, during COVID that they'll use any leverage they can against the United States and our interests around the globe.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
